  "Question": "The radius of \\(\\odot O\\) is \\(4\\). Points \\(A,B,C,D,E,F\\) divide the circumference into six equal parts. Find the length of chord \\(AB\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "4",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Using the usual convention that \\(A,B,C,D,E,F\\) are listed in cyclic order, \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) are adjacent division points. The central angle subtended by each arc is \\(360^\\circ\\div6=60^\\circ\\). Also, \\(OA=OB\\), so \\(\\triangle OAB\\) is equilateral. Therefore, \\(AB=OA=4\\).\n\nWithout the cyclic-order convention, \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) could instead be opposite division points, making \\(AB\\) a diameter of length \\(2\\cdot4=8\\). Thus \\(AB=4\\) under the recorded convention; without it, the length is not uniquely determined.",
